---
// Projects page - displays projects and work
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout>
	<main class="projects-content">
		
		<div class="project-item">
			<img src="/assets/Causal_Buddy.png" alt="Causal Buddy preview" class="project-image" />
			<div class="project-details">
				<h2><a href="https://causal-buddy.streamlit.app/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Causal Buddy</a></h2>
				<p>There are many great causal inference resources out already, but they don't provide a quick-hands-on way for students to play around with data, which really helps build intuition about the methods. So I built a platform that allows users to play around with simulated data. Check it out now!</p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<div class="project-item">
			<img src="/assets/CUPED.png" alt="CUPED Simulator preview" class="project-image" />
			<div class="project-details">
				<h2><a href="https://kevoinno.github.io/CUPED/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CUPED Simulator</a></h2>
				<p>This simulation tool helps PMs and data scientists build an intuition about how CUPED can reduce the time it takes to complete an A/B tests by several days.</p>
			</div>
		</div>

        <p>Please check out my <a href="https://github.com/kevoinno" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a> for more projects.</p>
	</main>
</Layout>

<style>
	.projects-content {
		line-height: 1.8;
		color: black;
		font-size: 24px;
	}
	
	.project-item {
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 20px;
		border: 2px solid black;
		border-radius: 8px;
		padding: 20px;
		margin-bottom: 30px;
	}

	.project-image {
		width: 260px;
		height: 200px;
		object-fit: contain;
		flex-shrink: 0;
	}

	.project-details {
		flex: 1;
	}

	.project-item h2 {
		font-size: 24px;
		margin: 0 0 8px 0;
		font-weight: 700;
	}

	.project-item h2 a {
		color: black;
		text-decoration: underline;
		transition: color 0.2s;
	}

	.project-item h2 a:hover {
		color: #555;
	}

	.projects-content p {
		margin-bottom: 16px;
		font-size: 18px;
	}
	
	.projects-content a {
		color: black;
		text-decoration: underline;
		transition: color 0.2s;
	}
	
	.projects-content a:hover {
		color: #555;
	}
</style>
